-void DmaPusher::RefreshSnapshot(CommandList& list, u64 now) {
+// The entries' sizes were fixed when the list was submitted, and so were the commands they hold:
+// memory can differ by now for three reasons. The game patched words in place before it released
+// an acquire (data words: the stream keeps its header words; Hyrule Warriors: Age of
+// Imprisonment), it submitted the list before it wrote it (Mario Kart World, Pokopia: upstream
+// 256b1dc346; those lists are copied during a suspension or are zeros at submit), or it already
+// recorded a later frame over the same command ring while the GPU thread ran frames behind
+// (Ocarina's pond, runs 162/247/282/293/298/299/306). The later recording's header words sit
+// elsewhere: a method runs past an entry's end into an unrelated entry (a call entry elsewhere in
+// memory), the parse slips a word, and the stream turns to junk.
+//
+// Without `check` (Push): memory's words, as T63. With it (a resume, Step), each entry from the
+// resume point on whose memory differs from its copy is walked both ways from the carry the stream
+// has there, and judged (RefreshVerdict):
+// - copy zeros where memory has commands: never written, memory;
+// - same header words: data only, memory; with EDEN_NX2_DESYNC_FIX, the copy once an entry earlier
+//   in this list was kept for a reshape (no later-frame data mixed into this frame's commands);
+// - other header words and the copy walks clean: with EDEN_NX2_DESYNC_FIX the copy, else memory;
+// - other header words, the copy drops words, memory doesn't: memory (the copy is the stale one);
+// - both drop words: memory, as T63, logged.
+// Lists copied during a suspension (odd count: 256b1dc346's lists), GPU-written and deferred
+// entries, and everything after a carry the walk can't know, take memory as T63 and are only
+// counted. Logged per resume (ReportRefreshCheck), bounded.
+void DmaPusher::RefreshSnapshot(CommandList& list, u64 now, RefreshCheck* check,
+                                size_t first_entry, size_t first_word) {
+    // Copied before this suspension began, or at an earlier resume: a copy that can be judged.
+    const bool judged_list = check != nullptr && (list.snapshot_suspensions & 1) == 0;
     list.snapshot_suspensions = now;
